## 5. PRE-OUTPUT CHECKLIST

Before generating README:
- [ ] Templates/examples read
- [ ] Mermaid diagrams planned (NOT ASCII)
- [ ] At least 2 diagrams included
- [ ] Badges use plain text format (NO external SVG)
- [ ] Sections match template
- [ ] R-GENIE attribution present

**If ANY check fails → DO NOT OUTPUT → Fix first**

---

## 6. EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every documentation decision must cite its source:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Section inclusion | "Including {section} — Template specifies include: true" |
| Project detail | "Version {X} — Extracted from pom.xml `<version>`" |
| Flow description | "Endpoint {path} — Found in {flow-file} `http:listener`" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Project file unclear on '{detail}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed facts.

---

## 7. TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in README generation:**
- API project vs batch project template selection
- System architecture vs flow process for primary diagram
- Which optional sections to include when template says "conditional"
- Level of technical detail in overview section

